OTOGAKURE FORBIDDEN TECHNIQUE ARCHIVE
CLASSIFICATION: RESTRICTED
Scroll Ref: FB-SN-009

SUBJECT: Senjutsu of the Ryuchi Cave — Snake Sage Mode (field notes)

Background
The Ryuchi Cave is one of the three great sage grounds. Its White Snake Sage confers
the serpent's senjutsu upon those who survive the transformation trial. Lord Orochimaru
pursued this path; the notes below are compiled from his study and from the disciple
line.

Observations
- Natural energy is drawn and balanced with one's own chakra to enter Sage Mode.
  Imbalance results in petrification — the body turns to stone. This risk is absolute.
- The snake senjutsu differs from the toad path (Myoboku) and the slug path; each sage
  ground is jealous of its own techniques.
- A practitioner who cannot hold the balance unaided may rely on a partnered summon or
  a shed-skin reservoir to stabilize intake.

Caution
This scroll is study material only. No Sound operative is cleared to attempt the
Ryuchi trial without Lord Orochimaru's express word. The petrification failure state is
irreversible by our medics.
